- input: |
  How should I style my components to support RTL languages?
  output: |
  To support RTL languages in your components:

  ✅ Use logical CSS properties instead of directional ones:

  ```css
  /* Good */
  .component {
    padding-inline-start: 1rem; /* Instead of padding-left */
    margin-inline-end: 0.5rem; /* Instead of margin-right */
    border-inline-start: 1px solid; /* Instead of border-left */
    text-align: start; /* Instead of text-align: left */
  }
  ```

  ✅ Import and use common UI color variables:

  ```css
  @use '@zencity/common-ui/styles/zcd-colors';

  .component {
    background: zcd-colors.$zcd-blue-20;
    color: zcd-colors.$zcd-gray-80;
  }
  ```

  ❌ Don't use directional properties:

  ```css
  /* Avoid */
  .component {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }
  ```

- input: |
  How should I handle spacing in my layouts?
  output: |
  For spacing in layouts:
  ✅ Use CSS variables for consistent spacing:

  ```scss
  :root {
    --space-xs: 4px;
    --space-sm: 8px;
    --space-md: 16px;
    --space-lg: 24px;
  }

  .component {
    padding: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  ```

  ✅ Use margin for spacing between elements and padding for internal spacing:

  ```scss
  .card {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md); /* Space between cards */
    padding: var(--space-md); /* Internal spacing */
  }
  ```

  ✅ Use flexbox/grid with gap for consistent spacing:

  ```scss
  .card-container {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }
  ```

  ❌ Don't use magic numbers or inconsistent spacing values
